  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Work is equal to area under <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> graph (when P is plotted along y-axis). As area under graph 3 is maximum and area under graph 1 is minimum, so <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is maximum and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is minimum.<br />So <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/786e3ce9-64ce-444a-9d24-1731b8c437efsdfbfalsdf.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 131px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
